FIND
====

Search for files by name.


BASIC
-----
find . -name "file.txt"

Searches current folder and subfolders.


OPTIONS
-------
Find by name:
  find . -name "*.js"

Search specific folder:
  find /home -name "photo.jpg"

Find directories:
  find . -type d -name "src"

Find files (not folders):
  find . -type f -name "*.py"


CASE INSENSITIVE
-----------------
find . -iname "FILE.txt"


EXECUTE COMMAND
---------------
find . -name "*.log" -delete

Deletes all .log files found.


TIPS
----
. = current directory
.. = parent directory
/ = root directory


EXAMPLE
-------
find . -name "*.txt"
find /home -name "project" -type d
find . -name "*.js" -type f
